1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,360
Your face flushes and burns all the time, and it's not just blushing - it might be rosacea.

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:12,320
Sun exposure, emotional stress, and heat are three of the biggest triggers, and getting to know yours can make a real difference.

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:21,840
Rosacea causes persistent redness and visible blood vessels on the cheeks, nose, and forehead, and it's often mistaken for acne or simply blushing easily.

4
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:26,320
In patient surveys, about a third report a flare-up every few days.

5
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:35,600
Sun exposure is the number one trigger - 81% of patients say it worsens their symptoms, because UV rays dilate and damage blood vessels under the skin.

6
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:40,640
Emotional stress is a close second, reported by 79% of patients.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:45,680
Stress hormones dilate blood vessels and trigger sudden flushing within minutes.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,960
Hot weather, wind, and heavy exercise round out the top triggers, each raising skin temperature and expanding facial vessels.

9
00:00:53,280 --> 00:01:03,840
Wear broad-spectrum SPF 30+ every morning and reapply outdoors, build in short stress breaks during the day, and exercise in cooler hours with a cold compress on hand.

10
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:12,640
More than 90% of patients who identify and avoid their personal triggers see real improvement - a dermatologist can help confirm what's actually going on.
